K1: one power-up per boot on janeiro, a wider KCI door, and its readback

These hunks apply to the edgetpu driver import in a development kernel tree. The
tree tracks only edgetpu-fs.c, edgetpu-pm.c and edgetpu.h under drivers/edgetpu/,
so the bring-up door and this change arrive as files rather than as history; the
patch is kept here so the change is reviewable and portable.

  edgetpu: janeiro: refuse a second power-up in the same boot

  After a power down the GSA/AON island stays unclocked (AON_RESET, AON_CLK,
  AON_QUIESCE and POWER_CONTROL all read 0xdeadfeed), GSA state stays 2 and the
  next power_up times out after 400 ms. Count the power-ups the boot has made and
  refuse the next request at once with -EBUSY, naming it in the log, instead of
  stalling the client for a timeout that cannot succeed.

  edgetpu: widen the KCI send door past one page

  KCI 16 (the firmware setup command) names a buffer larger than 4 KiB, and the
  door's descriptor size was capped at one page. The payload buffer and the
  iremap allocation now round up to the payload's size, so a 16 KiB command can
  be named.

  edgetpu: report the door's last return code

  A size sweep of one command reads the firmware's answer thousands of times;
  kci_last makes that a 4-byte read instead of a dmesg tail, so the sweep cannot
  miss an answer in a busy ring buffer.

--- a/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-pm.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 	/* Power up counter. Protected by @lock */
 	int power_up_count;
 	/* Total power-ups in this boot; never reset. Protected by @lock */
+	int power_up_total;
 	/* Flag indicating a deferred power down is pending. Protected by @lock */
 	bool power_down_pending;
 	/* Worker to handle async power down retry */
@@ -57,9 +58,23 @@
 		if (etpm->p->power_down_pending) {
 			etpm->p->power_down_pending = false;
 		} else {
+			/*
+			 * K1: the TPU does not come back in the same boot. After a power
+			 * down the GSA/AON island stays unclocked (AON_* read 0xdeadfeed)
+			 * and the next power_up times out. Refuse it at once, and say so,
+			 * instead of stalling a client for the whole timeout.
+			 */
+			if (etpm->p->power_up_total) {
+				etpm->p->power_up_count--;
+				etdev_err(etpm->etdev,
+					  "K1: power-up %d refused; the TPU cannot come back in this boot\n",
+					  etpm->p->power_up_total + 1);
+				return -EBUSY;
+			}
 			ret = etpm->p->handlers->power_up(etpm);
 			if (!ret) {
 				edgetpu_mailbox_restore_active_mailbox_queues(etpm->etdev);
+				etpm->p->power_up_total++;
 			}
 		}
 	}
--- a/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-fs.c
+++ b/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-fs.c
@@ -1070,17 +1070,26 @@
  * DMA descriptor, optionally carrying a payload. The KCI command set has no
